kill() of the CGI child when a request ends in an error had its arguments swapped:
kill(SIGTERM, pid) sent the signal numbered pid to the process 15 (or failed), and the
child was not stopped. Upstream pull request #44 (28.08.2017), as Gentoo carries it
(www-misc/fcgiwrap files/fcgiwrap-1.1.0-kill.patch).

--- fcgiwrap.c.orig
+++ fcgiwrap.c
@@ -206,7 +206,7 @@
 	if (fc->fd_stderr >= 0) close(fc->fd_stderr);
 
 	if (fc->cgi_pid)
-		kill(SIGTERM, fc->cgi_pid);
+		kill(fc->cgi_pid, SIGTERM);
 }
 
 static const char * fcgi_pass_fd(struct fcgi_context *fc, int *fdp, FCGI_FILE *ffp, char *buf, size_t bufsize)
